{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXG6XCnRm2uiS7ijapLd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Playback**\n\nI'm taking your recommended answers for all three rounds, and each one below is marked `assumed` where no source settled it.\n\n**Question and outcome**\n* Question: which step is a Roamstay damage claim at, who owes the next move and what status does it hold?\n* Outcome: support and product staff can place any claim on the board and name its next move and status. The reader is `assumed`. Your correction settles it.\n* Dials: Faithful detail, Mixed audience, Laptop distance\n\n**What the policy settled**\n* Lanes, in the order work reaches them: Hotel, Roamstay support, Guest, with a Claim status lane on top\n* Statuses: Reported, With the guest, Under review, Closed\n* Guest decision: accept or dispute within 7 days, and this is the accent\n* Support decision: uphold, which charges the card, or drop, within 5 working days\n* Dispute path: Under review while support reads the photos and the guest's reply\n* An uphold or a drop both end Closed\n\n**Assumed**\n* The charge steps sit in the Roamstay support lane. The policy says the card is charged but not who does it. Your correction settles it.\n* The accepted path ends at the charge with no status move. The policy gives an accepted claim no status after the charge, and \"either way\" follows the uphold and drop only. Your correction or the policy owner settles it.\n\n**Outline**\n1. Question: which step is a claim at, who owes the next move and what status does it hold?\n2. Hotel: Check-out, then Report damage. The report carries the photos and the repair quote, status Reported\n3. Roamstay support: Send claim to guest, status With the guest, carrying the photos and the quote\n4. Guest: Accept within 7 days? Exits: Accept, Dispute\n5. Accept goes to Roamstay support: Charge card on file, an end\n6. Dispute goes to Roamstay support: Review dispute, status Under review. It reads the photos and the guest's reply\n7. Roamstay support: Decide within 5 working days? Exits: Uphold, Drop\n8. Uphold goes to Charge card on file, then Claim closed. Drop goes to Drop the claim, then Claim closed, status Closed\n\nThat is 10 nodes, 4 statuses and 17 connectors, inside the 18 and 24 a laned Faithful board allows.\n\n**Framings**\n* Laned process with a status lane: shows who owes each move and the status at each step. It costs a wider board.\n* State map: shows every status and exit at a glance. It costs the hotel, guest and support split you asked for.\n* Recommended: the laned process, because you asked who it moves between and which status it holds.\n\n**Look**\n* Accent: the guest's Accept within 7 days? decision. The goal is Claim closed, named but not styled.\n* Zones: none, because the lanes are the zones\n* Title: Roamstay damage claim\n* Subtitle: From the hotel's damage report after check-out to a closed claim, for support and product staff\n* Source line: Roamstay claims policy. Left out: the under-25-euro waiver, not live\n\n**Left out and open**\n* The waiver for claims under 25 euros, because it is not live\n* What happens when the guest does not reply within 7 days, because the policy does not say\n* Whether an accepted claim closes after the charge, because the policy does not say\n\nThe board and the sketch come next. Is this reading right, or what should I correct?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3309,"cache_read_input_tokens":88256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3309},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b08072c8-af6d-4e0a-92ef-a4097c1ac96d","uuid":"5a1cbb25-8429-4f5a-86dd-11225418e303"